    // AiChatController.VerdictCache.cs -- v1.0.160.79
    // Partial of AiChatController holding the VERDICT CACHE: reuse a stored analysis instead of calling
    // the model again.
    //
    // In its OWN file, not appended to AiAudit.cs, deliberately. AiAudit is PASSIVE -- it records what
    // happened and can fail without changing a verdict. This code is ACTIVE: on a hit it SKIPS the model
    // call entirely. A subsystem that can change what an operator sees deserves to be reasoned about,
    // and reverted, on its own.
    //
    // SAFETY CONTRACT (do not weaken):
    //   * a cached verdict can be WRONG in a way a slow verdict never is -- an alert re-opened later has
    //     new telemetry, and the stored conclusion may no longer be supported. Staleness rules below are
    //     the substance of this file; the lookup is the trivial part;
    //   * ANY failure -- DB dormant, HTTP error, parse error, 404 -- falls through to a normal fresh
    //     analysis. Never an exception, never a blocked verdict;
    //   * a hit is always LABELLED. An operator must never receive a stored answer believing it is new.
